Adapted files (layouts and packet encoders rewritten in Rust, not copied line by line):

- hypercolor-openrgb-sdk/src/parser.rs  -> crates/canvas-adapters/src/protocol.rs
  (OpenRGB controller-data field order; mode, zone and segment layouts; v4/v5 conditionals)
- hypercolor-openrgb-sdk/src/packet.rs  -> crates/canvas-adapters/src/protocol.rs
  (packet ids; UPDATELEDS, RESIZEZONE, SET_CLIENT_NAME, REQUEST_PROTOCOL_VERSION payloads;
  protocol version constants)
- hypercolor-openrgb-sdk/src/types.rs   -> crates/canvas-adapters/src/openrgb.rs
  (OpenRGB device-type and zone-type raw mapping)
- hypercolor-windows-pawnio/src/windows.rs -> crates/canvas-svc/src/pawnio.rs
  (PawnIO C entry-point names and argument shapes; THM_TCON_CUR_TMP decode constants)
- The DeviceAdapter trait shape (crates/canvas-proto/src/traits.rs) follows Hypercolor's
  DeviceBackend.

Facts only, no code copied (cited in comments): register addresses for the Nuvoton NCT6687D-R
from the nct6687d Linux driver (GPL) and LibreHardwareMonitor's Nct677X.cs (MPL-2.0); PawnIO
LpcIO module ioctl names from PawnIO.Modules (GPL-2.0), used through PawnIO's IOCTL interface.

